+### GPU Implementation Architecture
+*   **What it is**: The general architectural design for implementing volume rendering on GPUs, including memory hierarchies and shader models [G].
+*   **Difference**: The multithreaded pipeline is a specific optimization technique for pipelined hardware (often FPGA or custom ASIC), whereas GPU architecture is a broader framework that may use different parallelism models (SIMT) [G].
+*   **When to choose**: Use when designing the overall system for a GPU, rather than optimizing a specific pipelined hardware unit [G].
+*   **Link**: [GPU Implementation Architecture](11245-gpu-implementation-architecture.md)
